./logs/iter_001_synthesis.stderr.log:2128:iterations/iter_001/idea_03/critic_02_on_explorer_02.md:18:   The delayed-grid reduction assumes the learner can reconstruct the full truncated reward vector for all grid quotes after delay `H` from observed prices. This is true if every `P_t` is revealed and the price process is exogenous/counterfactual rewards are well-defined. It is not automatic in a pure bandit/trade-only feedback model.
