./logs/iter_004_synthesis.stderr.log:5062:+- Masoudian, Zimmert, and Seldin (NeurIPS/OpenReview 2024) is verified. Its abstract explicitly frames the complexity of delayed bandits in terms of information missing at decision time, measured by outstanding observations, rather than elapsed delay. This is conceptually well aligned with replacing raw \(\beta\)-tails by missing-information or skipped-feedback quantities.
