./logs/iter_010_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:1378:Invalid as stated. The identity that a zero-block quote \(A_s\) has traded by \(T_j\) iff \(A_s<c_j\) uses \(0<c_1<\cdots<c_m\) in path order. If the thresholds are unsorted, the effective threshold by \(T_j\) is \(\max_{\ell\le j}c_\ell\), and the \(\kappa(C)\) formula for the displayed order no longer follows directly.
./logs/iter_010_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:1541:at horizon \(T_2=N+2\), a zero-block action \(A_s=3/4\) has already traded at the first threshold \(1\). But \(A_s<c_2\) is false when \(c_2=1/2\). Thus the zero-block learner payoff by \(T_j\) is governed by \(\max_{\ell\le j}c_\ell\), not by the displayed \(c_j\), unless the path order is increasing.
./logs/iter_010_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:1611:- Masoudian, Zimmert, and Seldin (NeurIPS/OpenReview 2024) is verified. Its abstract explicitly frames the complexity of delayed bandits in terms of information missing at decision time, measured by outstanding observations, rather than elapsed delay. This is conceptually well aligned with replacing raw \(\beta\)-tails by missing-information or skipped-feedback quantities.
./logs/iter_010_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:1629:- Maran and Restelli (arXiv:2605.19584, COLT 2026 accepted-papers page) is verified. It studies online market making with action-dependent order-book feedback and regret guarantees. Adjacent terminology and feedback-structure contrast only; it is not the same delayed-fill tail problem.
./logs/iter_010_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:1630:- Roesler and Szentes (AER 2017), Shen-Tang-Zeng (AAMAS 2018), and Condorelli-Szentes (JPE 2020) are verified equal-revenue/monopoly-pricing sources. They support the \(1/e\) posted-price surplus geometry used in the multi-threshold \(\kappa\) dual, but they do not prove market-making lower bounds.
./logs/iter_010_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:1652:- Blackwell (Pacific J. Math. 1956) and Sion (Pacific J. Math. 1958) are verified as classical approachability/minimax references. They are relevant only as conceptual/minimax support for the prefix-compatibility LP; the market-making transfer still needs a direct proof.
