./logs/iter_006_synthesis.stderr.log:1297:- Masoudian, Zimmert, and Seldin (NeurIPS/OpenReview 2024) is verified. Its abstract explicitly frames the complexity of delayed bandits in terms of information missing at decision time, measured by outstanding observations, rather than elapsed delay. This is conceptually well aligned with replacing raw \(\beta\)-tails by missing-information or skipped-feedback quantities.
./logs/iter_006_synthesis.stderr.log:1326:- Blackwell (Pacific J. Math. 1956) and Sion (Pacific J. Math. 1958) are verified as classical approachability/minimax references. They are relevant only as conceptual/minimax support for the prefix-compatibility LP; the market-making transfer still needs a direct proof.
./logs/iter_006_synthesis.stderr.log:1380:- Pooria Joulani, Andras Gyorgy, Csaba Szepesvari. "Delay-Tolerant Online Convex Optimization: Unified Analysis and Adaptive-Gradient Algorithms." Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence 30(1), 2016. DOI: https://doi.org/10.1609/aaai.v30i1.10320. Relevance: full-information delayed-feedback/OCO reduction and adaptive-gradient algorithms; possible support for cleaner grid sufficiency variants.
./logs/iter_006_synthesis.stderr.log:1402:- Jacob Abernethy, Peter L. Bartlett, Elad Hazan. "Blackwell Approachability and No-Regret Learning are Equivalent." COLT 2011, PMLR 19:27-46. https://proceedings.mlr.press/v19/abernethy11b.html. Relevance: possible framework for simultaneous constraint feasibility or prefix-compatibility formulations.
./logs/iter_006_synthesis.stderr.log:1432:- Shan Xue, Ye Du, Liang Xu. "Adaptive Market Making with Inventory Constraints via Online Learning." Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence 39(20):21859-21867, 2025. https://doi.org/10.1609/aaai.v39i20.35492. Relevance: adjacent online-learning market-making model with inventory constraints; not a delayed-fill tail characterization.
./logs/iter_006_synthesis.stderr.log:1436:- David Blackwell. "An analog of the minimax theorem for vector payoffs." Pacific Journal of Mathematics 6(1):1-8, 1956. https://msp.org/pjm/1956/6-1/p01.xhtml. Relevance: classical origin of approachability/vector-payoff feasibility; conceptual background for prefix-compatibility formulations.
./logs/iter_006_synthesis.stderr.log:1440:- Joon Kwon, Vianney Perchet. "Online Learning and Blackwell Approachability with Partial Monitoring: Optimal Convergence Rates." AISTATS 2017, PMLR 54:604-613. https://proceedings.mlr.press/v54/kwon17a.html. Relevance: approachability with partial monitoring and multi-criteria objectives; possible framework for dynamic prefix-compatibility variants.
